  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLOCATION AND BLOCK PLANS  E 00\rPROPOSED DRAWINGS FLOOR PLANS P 01\rPROPOSED DRAWINGS FLOOR PLANS P 02\rPROPOSED DRAWINGS ELEVATIONS P 03\rPROPOSED DRAWINGS ELEVATIONS P 04\rPROPOSED DRAWINGS SECTION P 05\rPROPOSED DRAWINGS DETAILS P 06\rPROPOSED DRAWINGS DETAILS P 07\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.",
    "The external finishing materials shall match those used in the construction of the existing building and/or areas of hard surfacing. \r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of five people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to\rsafeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.",
    "No additional independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen/dining room shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.",
    "The cycle and refuse storage details hereby approved shall be provided prior to the occupation of the development and thereafter permanently maintained to the satisfaction of the Local Planning Authority unless otherwised agreed in writing.\r\rReason: To encourage sustainable means of transport, to provide secure cycle storage and waste disposal facilities and in the interest of visual amenity."
  ],
